Lets the host replace the decoded PCM of XMA streams it recognises through rex_audio_set_xma_pcm_provider. The guest keeps decoding the original packets, so length, loops, stalls and stops are unchanged; only the samples written to the output ring differ, and a stream the provider does not know, a mono stream or a provider failure keeps the decoded audio. State is at file scope because the exe compiles against the stock header.

